 "category_zh": "石窟艺术",
 "category_en": "Grotto art",
 "intro_zh": "龙门石窟位于洛阳市城南十三公里，始凿于北魏孝文帝年间，盛于唐，终于清末。历经10多个朝代陆续营造长达1400余年，是世界上营造时间最长的石窟。石窟密布于伊水东西两山的峭壁上，南北长达1公里，现存窟龛2345个，题记和碑刻2680余品，佛塔70余座，造像10万余尊。",
 "intro_en": "The Longmen Grottoes are located 13 kilometers south of Luoyang City. They were first excavated during the reign of Emperor Xiaowen of the Northern Wei Dynasty, flourished in the Tang Dynasty, and ended in the late Qing Dynasty. It has been built for more than 1,400 years in more than 10 dynasties, making it the longest grotto in the world. The grottoes are densely distributed on the cliffs of the east and west mountains of Yishui, with a length of 1 kilometer from north to south. There are 2,345 cave niches, more than 2,680 inscriptions and tablets, more than 70 pagodas, and more than 100,000 statues.",
 "intro_en_source": "machine_translation",
